Baseline: login takes 400ms p95. Target: under 100ms. Hot path: createSession below. Constraint: session format unchanged.

```js
async function createSession(user) {
  const token = Math.random().toString(36).slice(2)
  const all = await db.sessions.findAll()
  if (all.some(s => s.token === token)) return createSession(user)
  await db.sessions.insert({ token, userId: user.id })
  return token
}
```

What to transform: the duplicated discount calculation in both branches. Extract it.
What must not change: the public signature of price() and every return value.
Scope: this function only.
Why: duplicated logic (DRY); the two copies already drifted once.

```js
export function price(user, amount) {
  if (user.isAdmin) {
    const d = amount > 100 ? amount * 0.1 : 0
    return Math.round((amount - d) * 100) / 100
  } else {
    const d = amount > 100 ? amount * 0.1 : 0
    return Math.round((amount - d) * 100) / 100 + 2
  }
}
```

